{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_slice_6b", "label": "Slice 6b \u2014 The Part You Clicked, and a Grid That Holds a Thousand", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The premise was wrong once already: the grid is not slow, it is incomplete. Measured at 16 ms warm against an 80 ms budget, while fetchParts asked for one page and never asked for another, so a library of 1,000 parts showed 50. Paging is the requirement; virtualization is the optimization it enables."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_infinite_query_paging", "label": "useInfiniteQuery Cursor Paging", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "PartsPage.next is already a PartId or null, which is exactly getNextPageParam's contract, so nothing on the server changes. More pages are fetched by an IntersectionObserver sentinel rather than a button, because a grid is a scrolling surface and the gesture that means 'show me more' is scrolling to the end of it."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_content_visibility_auto", "label": "content-visibility: auto Instead of a Virtualizer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A virtualizer is a dependency, a measured scroll container, and a fight with a responsive auto-fill grid whose column count changes with the viewport. One CSS rule measured 8.8 ms against 128.4 ms for a cold full-page scroll pass over 1,000 cards \u2014 14.6x, no dependency, and the grid stays a plain CSS grid. contain-intrinsic-size is 26rem, not the 20rem first guessed from a card measured before its thumbnail loaded."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_tessellation_l0_on_card", "label": "PartSummary.tessellation_l0", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Without it the L0 glTF every ingest writes is unreachable and GET /api/blob/{blake3} has no possible caller. It is a hash, not a URL, and holding it is not authorization \u2014 derivative_is_reachable is what makes the field safe to hand out."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_detail_route", "label": "GET /api/parts/{id} \u2014 PartDetail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Every mesh-derived figure goes over the wire as {value, provenance} rather than a bare number with a badge computed beside it, because a bare number with a separate boolean is how the label gets lost when B-rep figures arrive on the same part in Phase 2. An open mesh reports no volume at all, in words."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_sse_batch_events", "label": "SSE Batch Events Stream", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "react-query does not poll a hidden document, so the progress line froze on a hidden tab. It is LISTEN/NOTIFY with a timer floor, for the reason slice 2 wrote down. The stream ends itself when the batch does, because EventSource reconnects automatically and a stream that merely goes quiet is one the browser will re-open forever. The poll stays as the fallback."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_seeded_example_part", "label": "Migration-Seeded Example Part", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A migration cannot mesh, so the seeded part carries its measurements and thumbnail as committed literals. It is a normal part, not a special one: no is_example column, no filter that hides it, no first-run flag \u2014 the row is the same shape ingest writes, so nothing downstream needs to know it arrived differently."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_live_fill_gated_on_first_page", "label": "The Live-Fill Refetch Is Gated on Grid Depth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "invalidateQueries on an infinite query refetches every page it holds, so the settle-effect pulled eleven pages per tick \u2014 roughly 4.7 MB a second \u2014 and bought nothing, because parts arrive newest-first ahead of every cursor already held. Trimming the cache to one page would be the other way, and it snaps a reading user back to the top."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_gallery_deferred", "label": "The part_image Gallery Leaves Phase 1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Slice 4's argument \u2014 user data cannot live in SourceStore or DerivativeStore \u2014 is dissolved by the folder-tree layout, where a model becomes a real directory holding an images/ folder. The gallery belongs to whichever slice lands that layout, where it is one directory listing rather than a migration, an upload route and a UI rewritten weeks later."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_slice_6b", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_slice_6a", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_infinite_query_paging", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_content_visibility_auto", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_infinite_query_paging", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_live_fill_gated_on_first_page", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_tessellation_l0_on_card", "target": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_part_summary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_tessellation_l0_on_card", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_blob_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6b-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6b_design_tessellation_l0_on_card", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_reachabi